2026-10-16T03:57:46.5860867Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 55937
2026-10-16T03:57:46.5861212Z   ISSUE_TITLE: core: global location watcher subscribes to all of $HOME — 2M+ file home dirs starve the event loop (~900% CPU, multi-GB memory), /api/model 503
2026-10-16T03:57:46.5866566Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Environment

- opencode: **v2.0.30** (also reproduced on v2.0.21; both installed via npm `@opencode/cli`)
- OS: macOS 26.6.2 (Tahoe, Build 25G83), Apple Silicon M4 (arm64)
- Zero user plugins, zero custom providers, brand-new config (fully reproducible with a pristine `HOME`)

## Symptoms

1. `opencode serve` boots fine, then the server process pins **300–900% CPU** and memory keeps climbing to **several GB** (`%mem` ~20% and rising). It never recovers.
2. `GET /api/model` hangs until the location-plugin activation timeout and returns **503 "Location plugins did not finish activating"** — hence the TUI shows "No items available" in the model picker and "No provider selected".
3. On v2.0.21 the blowup is **deferred to the first chat message**: as soon as a message is sent, the server child process hits ~587% CPU + multiple GB RSS, and the TUI logs `Timed out connecting` repeatedly, then shows "Connection lost… Reconnecting".
4. TUI↔server SSE repeatedly logs `Event stream stalled` → "Restarting service…" loops, even with all proxy env vars unset.

## Debug-log evidence (v2.0.30, `--log-level debug`)

The server's location watcher subscribes to **the entire home directory and filesystem root**:

```
watcher subscribe path=/ type=entries ignores=0 role=server
watcher subscribe path=/private type=entries ignores=0
watcher subscribe path=/Library/Application Support type=entries ignores=0
watcher subscribe path=/Users/chuan type=entries ignores=0     <-- $HOME
watcher subscribe path=/Users/chuan/.config/opencode type=directory
```

This machine's `$HOME` contains **2,130,792 files** (iCloud Drive sync + years of dev projects). After the watcher subscribes, CPU explodes (sampled while at ~900% CPU: all hot samples burn inside JIT-compiled JS frames, no native symbol names available).

## Decisive A/B experiment

| Run | `$HOME` file count | Server CPU | `GET /api/model` |
|---|---|---|---|
| Real home | **2,130,792** | 909% peak → ~330% sustained, memory climbing | **503**, activation timeout |
| Fake empty home (`env HOME=/tmp/oc-home opencode serve`) | 0 | **0.0–0.2%** | **200 OK in 165 ms**, full free-model list returned |

```bash
# reproduce (A: broken)
opencode serve &
curl -u "opencode:$PW" http://127.0.0.1:4096/api/model   # 503 after activation timeout, CPU pinned

# reproduce (B: healthy)
env HOME=$(mktemp -d) opencode serve &
curl -u "opencode:$PW" http://127.0.0.1:4096/api/model   # 200 OK in 165 ms
```

## Relation to #55272

Same failure shape (CPU-heavy work starving the shared event loop → HTTP/SSE stall), but **completely different trigger surface**: this reproduces with **zero user plugins** — no 30×3 native-plugin fixture needed. The trigger is the global location watcher subscribing to `$HOME`/`/` on machines where those trees are huge. Likely same root (event-loop starvation), different entry point.

## Expected fix / ask

- Don't recursively watch the whole `$HOME` (and `/`) by default, or
- provide an escape hatch (env var / config) to disable or scope the global location watcher, or
- make the initial watch scan incremental/async so it cannot starve the shared event loop.

Happy to provide `sample` call-stack dumps or any further data points.

